# story/01-arrival.scene — bible.md spine scenes 1-2 (Hook, First
# loader). Kept lines are cited inline with their source. See
# docs/canon/bible.md and docs/canon/kept.md.

== start
bg desert_night
show slim neutral left
# kept: script.rpy:78
slim: Sure is getting cold out here on Syntax-4. The triple moons are all up - gonna be a bright night.
> A satellite hums somewhere overhead, hunting for a lock.
show terminal idle right
# kept: script.rpy:119
slim: (sudo restart satellite)
# kept: script.rpy:122
terminal: Welcome, root. Please enter password:
terminal: Accepted. Handshake complete.
> Best pass the wait telling it something true.
choice
    "Talk about the climb up from the orbital yards." -> origin_cosmonaut
    "Talk about growing up on dirt, fixing what breaks." -> origin_cowboy
    "Talk about the year spent only talking to machines." -> origin_coder

== origin_cosmonaut
set origin = 0, cosmonaut = 2, cowboy = 1, coder = 1
slim: Trained on a station with a view and no horizon. Down here, the horizon's the whole job.
-> muster

== origin_cowboy
set origin = 1, cosmonaut = 1, cowboy = 2, coder = 1
slim: Grew up patching fence and engines with whatever was on hand. A link loader's just a fence that thinks.
-> muster

== origin_coder
set origin = 2, cosmonaut = 1, cowboy = 1, coder = 2
slim: Spent a year out past the relay towers with nobody but the machines for company. Learned to like the quiet parens make.
-> muster

== muster
# kept: script.rpy:172
terminal: git pull: Loading new coordinates and repair protocols...
# kept: script.rpy:175
slim: Finally! This connection is slower than a turtle in molasses.
terminal: Diagnostic package staged. Confirm load?
# kept: script.rpy:190
slim: Yes, and run a diagnostic on our repair tools. We'll need the parenthesis patcher and the recursion breaker for sure.
# kept: script.rpy:181 (the "won't link themselves" title pun)
slim: Alright, time to head out. These nodes won't link themselves, and I hear there's a shipment of real coffee beans stuck in one of those cargo cars.
choice
    "Call Clipi in before heading out." -> call_clipi
    "Head out first. Loop Clipi in from the field." -> head_out

== call_clipi
show clipi talk center
clipi: Online and current, Slim. Say the word and I'm in the loop.
set met_clipi = true
hide terminal
-> loader_site

== head_out
hide terminal
> Terminal goes quiet behind. Clipi stays dark for now.
-> loader_site

== loader_site
show slim talk left
> The loader squats at the rail joint, coupling arm locked half open. A cargo bot stands over it, patient as stone, waiting on a chain that will not close.
# kept: script.rpy:240
cargo_bot: (Sh-query maintenance status sh-current sh-loader)
if origin == 0
    > The half-open arm reminds Slim of yard couplings — cleaner work, kinder gravity.
if origin == 1
    > The half-open arm reminds Slim of fence wire. Same stubborn geometry, no atmosphere to speak of.
if origin == 2
    > The half-open arm reminds Slim of a terminal left running too long. Patient, and past reasoning with.
if met_clipi
    show clipi talk center
    clipi: Buoy's been repeating itself for an hour. Words, not code yet. Read it before you touch the arm.
else
    > A handheld chirps on Slim's belt. The Fen buoy, saying the same five words over and over.
puzzle decode-buoy
    pass -> transmission_clear
    lockout -> transmission_garbled

== transmission_clear
slim: Signal, star, dust, drift, home. Just a beacon riding stardust, calling for harbor. This loader's not broken. It's flinching at an echo.
> The fix, once you know it's an echo and not a break, takes ten minutes.
show slim laughing left
slim: Clean bind, first try. Some jobs are just jobs.
-> sabotage_evidence

== transmission_garbled
> Two words come through clean: signal, home. The rest stays static.
> Slim fixes the arm by hand, the slow way, without the buoy's warning to go on.
set messy_fix = true
show slim frown left
slim: Held. Didn't need to be pretty.
-> sabotage_evidence
